{
 "title": "Hold-fix NIS limit on --preset urban; why urban publishes fewer epochs",
 "doc": "docs/rtk_hold_fix_nis.md",
 "reference_use": "The reference trajectory is used only for scoring and the analysis-only phase audit.",
 "frozen_rule": "Frozen before the replay (2026-10-26). Branch fix/rtk-hold-fix-history on develop 8c399b40 (#661).\nChange: opt-in RTKConfig::hold_fix_max_update_nis_per_observation (CLI --hold-fix-max-update-nis-per-obs, default 0 = off):\nreject a hold-fix candidate (\"hold_fix_update_nis\") when the same epoch's float update NIS per observation exceeds it.\nReproduction: RTKHoldFixDefaultTest.HoldFixIgnoresAnInconsistentFloatUpdateUnlessItsNisLimitIsSet (legacy accepts a hold\nfix after an update with NIS 52.5, the Shinjuku TOW 281650.1 value).\nValue: 10, the value of the existing AR-only fixed-update NIS gate experiments (docs/ppc_realtime_gate_existing_outputs.md,\nfixed_nis10); not tuned here. Disclosed: before choosing, the urban (CDME) debug logs on the 10 runs were examined:\naccepted correct FIX NIS p99 10.2; genuine wrong FIX NIS p50 9.7; 183 of 256 genuine wrong FIX are hold fixes, 107 of them\nwith NIS > 10; direct cost of a hold-only limit 10 = 0.0-0.7% of correct FIX on 9 runs and 12.0% on PPC nagoya/run3.\nRecipes: U = --preset urban (baseline, = CDME); UH = U + --hold-fix-max-update-nis-per-obs 10. Both on the new binary.\nRuns: Trimble/u-blox Odaiba/Shinjuku, PPC tokyo/nagoya run1-3 (bare argv), HK Deep/Harsh (descriptive).\nScoring as the CDMEH round; phase audit (decision_rule_phase_audit.txt) on Trimble and PPC.\nGates (per run):\n A: UH vs RTKLIB demo5 multi-GNSS: more FIX and wrong >0.5/2/3 m each <= RTKLIB (audited where available, raw elsewhere).\n W: audited (raw for u-blox) wrong >0.5/2/3 m not increased vs U on any run, and the 10-run audited wrong >0.5 m total decreases.\n L: U-correct loss <= 1%.\n M: missing epochs and horizontal P95 not increased.\nDecision: A and W and L and M on every run -> propose adding the flag to --preset urban.\n A and W pass but L or M fail somewhere -> report the trade to the user; no preset change without the user's decision.\n A or W fails -> NO_GO (stays opt-in).\nPredictions: P1 Shinjuku Trimble confirmed wrong (audit) 69 -> <= 20. P2 10-run audited wrong >0.5 m total falls by >= 30%.\n P3 L fails on PPC nagoya/run3 and passes on the other runs. P4 default and U POS byte-identical to develop on Trimble\n Odaiba and Shinjuku (flag off).\nNo retuning after the replay.\n",
 "frozen_rule_sha256": "82671dacb4835f12c65dff83961d4ef2f48d3de74e8582fbeaad1edfc67f57e7",
 "binary": {
  "source": "fix/rtk-hold-fix-nis f910e68c (develop 8c399b40 + the option)",
