 "variant_keep_hold_run": {
  "frozen_rule": "Frozen before the replay (2026-10-26). Branch fix/rtk-hold-fix-nis (PR #663) plus the variant; develop 8c399b40 base.\nChange: opt-in RTKConfig::hold_fix_update_nis_keeps_hold_run (CLI --hold-fix-update-nis-keeps-hold-run, default off).\nA hold fix rejected only by hold_fix_max_update_nis_per_observation keeps the hold path open: the fix run it had\n(nis_suspended_hold_run_) still counts for canAttemptHoldFix and for applyHoldAmbiguity until a fix extends the run\npast it, any other hold rejection, a reacquisition reset, an SPP fallback or a FLOAT epoch without that rejection\nends it. consecutive_fix_count_ and its other uses (fix-history check etc.) are unchanged.\nTests: RTKHoldFixDefaultTest.NisRejectedHoldKeepsTheHoldPathOpenOnlyWhenAsked,\nKeptHoldRunEndsAtAnyOtherHoldRejection (written before the code; did not build without it).\nMotivation (UH debug logs): nagoya/run3: 97 of 104 lost U-correct fixes are U hold fixes that UH never attempted\n(hold path closed after a NIS rejection); tokyo/run2: most of 230 are AR fixes that no longer resolved.\nRecipes: U = --preset urban; UH = U + --hold-fix-max-update-nis-per-obs 10; UH2 = UH + --hold-fix-update-nis-keeps-hold-run.\nAll on the new binary. Runs, scoring and the phase audit as the UH round (decision_rule_holdnis.txt).\nGates for UH2 (per run, vs U unless stated): A vs RTKLIB (audited where available); W wrong >0.5/2/3 m not increased and\n10-run audited total decreases; L U-correct loss <= 1%; M missing and Hp95 not increased. Reported next to UH.\nDecision: A, W, L, M on every run -> propose adding both flags to --preset urban (the user decides).\n A and W pass, L or M fail somewhere -> report the trade (vs U and vs UH) to the user; the preset is unchanged.\n A or W fails -> NO_GO.\nPredictions: P1 nagoya/run3 U-correct loss < 5% (UH 9.90%). P2 10-run audited wrong >0.5 m <= 160 (UH 142, U 256).\n P3 L still fails on at least one PPC run. P4 U and UH POS byte-identical to the UH round (flag off).\nNo retuning after the replay.\n",
